(The text form of test 859: after the branch, the name is the top-level
 buffer, and passing it to a buffer parameter grows that buffer.)
a buffer called hold is "abc".

To 'grow' with a buffer called data.
    For each k from 1 to 3000, append "abcdefgh" to data.

To 'branchy' with a number called n.
    If n is 1 then,
        a text called hold is "local",
        Print "in branch {hold}".
    'grow' of hold.
    Print "after branch {hold's size}".

'branchy' of 1.
'branchy' of 2.
Print "top {hold's size}".
